  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is hanging from one end of a uniform rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> pivoted at its end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> on a vertical wall as shown in figure. It is supported by a cable <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> such that the system is in equilibrium. The tension in the cable is:</p><p>(Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0087_6cb9b9807ae5.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 397px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
